ngerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas. Strengths: anticipation (decision quality, safety), complex connections (technical competence), spatial vision (pilot), leadership. Weaknesses: show-off (crew cooperation), not open to new ideas (adaptability). No mention of stress resilience.\n\nCandidate D: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration, adaptability to unexpected. Weaknesses: hot temper (crew cooperation, professional communication), know-it-all (crew cooperation). No explicit stress resilience.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely Candidate A has strong decision speed and calm, but communication issues severe for crew. Candidate B has good reliability and stress, but interpersonal issues. Candidate C has strong anticipation and leadership but not open to ideas. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but hot temper.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate A's calm and quick decisions are crucial for long-distance, but communication is vital. Candidate B's nasty remarks are serious. Candidate C's not open to new ideas could hinder adaptability. Candidate D's hot temper is serious.\n\nMaybe Candidate A is still best despite communication issues? But egocentric and difficulty communicating could be fatal. Candidate B's nasty remarks also severe. Candidate C's show-off maybe less severe than nasty remarks? Show-off may affect crew but maybe manageable. Not open to new ideas is a concern for long-distance where varied conditions. Candidate D's hot temper is serious.\n\nThus maybe Candidate C is best overall: strong anticipation, technical, leadership, decision quality. Show-off and not open to new ideas are concerns but perhaps less severe than egocentric or nasty remarks. So I might recommend Candidate C.\n\nWe need to state recommendation and give evidence. Also note that we haven't discussed others yet, but we can start with Candidate C. Provide vote = Candidate C.\n\nLet's craft public message: mention that I think Candidate C stands out due to anticipation, complex connections, leadership, which are critical for safety and decision quality. Acknowledge concerns (show-off, not open) but weigh against others' interpersonal issues. So vote for C.\n\nProceed."}
